Limitations (what you should criticize in your presentation)

Congestion signal is very weak/indirect. The counter is incremented when a flagged RREP passes (route establishment) — that doesn’t directly measure queue length, MAC retries, channel busy time, or actual packet service rate. So “busy” is only approximated.

Threshold choice is underspecified. They rely on a “predetermined value” threshold (and even say future work is optimizing it). 

CC-ADOV_An_effective_multiple_p…

 Without an adaptive rule, results can swing a lot.

Dropping RREQs can reduce reachability. If too many nodes drop RREQs, route discovery can fail more often, or force longer detours → higher delay (which they indeed observe).

Overhead is claimed but not quantified. They state overhead exists (extra header field + routing-table logic), but they don’t report control overhead metrics (RREQ/RREP/RERR counts, bytes, MAC retransmissions). 

CC-ADOV_An_effective_multiple_p…

Power metric is a bit questionable. They frame “each received consumption power” and compare total power but it’s not clear whether full radio energy model is used consistently; power also doesn’t improve much.



